  "term": "asthenopia",
  "definition": "Asthenopia is visual weakness in which the eyes tire easily, especially because the muscles used for focusing or moving the eyes are prone to fatigue. It may arise from strain or weakness in those eye mechanisms, or as part of a more general bodily disorder.",
